    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Base class for switch actions.</para><para>These objects represent some action that occurs after all switches are parsed and the <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1CommandLine_1_1ParserResult_1acaf0cc3098ff5eb9d84009e1f05ebf4c" kindref="member">ParserResult::apply</ref> method is called.</para><para>Actions are always allocated on the heap and reference counted. Each action defines a class factory method, <computeroutput>instance</computeroutput>, to allocate a new object and return a pointer to it. The pointer types are named <computeroutput>Ptr</computeroutput> and are defined within the class. For convenience, the actions built into the library also have global factory functions which have the same name as the class but start with an initial lower-case letter (see <ref refid="group__sawyer__action__factories" kindref="compound">Command line action factories</ref> for details). For instance:</para><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">SwitchAction::Ptr<sp/>action1<sp/>=<sp/>UserAction::instance&lt;MyFunctor&gt;(myFunctor);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">SwitchAction::Ptr<sp/>action2<sp/>=<sp/>userAction(myFunctor);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
